--- DR-0063: a run is governed by a SET of signed envelopes, one per party
--- authority, and the effective policy is their MEET. The record defines
--- composition by refusal rather than by schema:
---
---   C1  check(P, meet(S)) accepts  =>  every e in S accepts.
---
--- That is a one-way implication and it is the whole content of the design. A
--- meet that refuses where a constituent accepts is fine -- stricter is always
--- allowed. A meet that ACCEPTS where a constituent REFUSES is a party's policy
--- being overridden by someone it never authorized, which is the failure the
--- record exists to make impossible.
---
--- WHAT THIS MODEL IS FOR. C1 is a theorem about the composition function, not a
--- definition of it, so the model must make the function concrete enough to get
--- wrong. Composition therefore runs over the envelope ARMS, and the
--- per-envelope (solo) verdict is computed by the SAME shared equations in every
--- module below. Only the composed half varies. A sibling that composes one arm
--- the other way then produces a state carrying `admitted(X)` and
--- `soloRefuses(A, X)` together, which is a literal C1 counterexample rather
--- than an argument about one.
---
--- THE TWO DUAL-GATED FIELDS COMPOSE IN OPPOSITE DIRECTIONS, and getting that
--- backwards is the mistake this model exists to catch. The record's general
--- rule: at a crossing the kernel asks `dominates(provider, required)`, so the
--- `required` side composes by union and the `provider` side by intersection.
---
---   readers   is a CONJUNCTIVE COMPARTMENT SET -- a party reads only if it
---             acts-for EVERY compartment (`reader_set` in ifc.rs, proved in
---             models/lean/Whipple/ReaderSets.lean, where union is the join and
---             the empty set is the public bottom). As a source tag it therefore
---             composes by UNION. Intersecting two envelopes' compartments
---             widens: A::Operator intersect B::Auditor is empty, which is
---             public, a label both constituents refuse.
---   vouchers  are the provider side at a sink, so a source tag composes by
---             INTERSECTION -- data is only as trusted as the LEAST-trusting
---             party, and A vouching for A's own data does not bind B. Sink
---             demands compose by union, being the `required` side.
---
--- The model covers the SOURCE reading of both fields and the SINK reading of
--- integrity. The sink reading of readers is the mirror of the source reading of
--- vouchers and is not separately modelled; that is an honest limit, not a claim
--- that it needs no rule.
---
--- DOWNGRADE GRANTS ARE OWNED, NOT COMPOSED (section 3), and "not composed" has
--- to be read INSIDE the fold: a grant clears the compartments of the envelope
--- that ISSUED it and no others. On a resource two envelopes both label, a grant
--- applied to the composed label would clear its co-owner's compartment as well,
--- which is a party's policy being overridden by someone it never authorized --
--- the very thing ownership is meant to prevent. Passing the ownership check is
--- therefore not enough; the issuer must still be known when the grant applies.
---
--- THE COMPOSITION RECORD IS EVIDENCE (section 4), so it must name exactly the
--- set the run was checked under. A record short of the composition is the
--- omission section 4 calls the attack; an entry for an authority the
--- composition does not carry evidences an envelope that never applied; and two
--- entries for one authority leave the checked epoch undetermined. There is no
--- default entry -- a constituent the record does not name is refused, because a
--- defaulted entry is a policy version nobody stated.
---
--- Grounding, against the shipped envelope schema in
--- spec/information-flow-governance.md:
---   readers(R, RS)     confidentiality compartments on a resource this envelope
---                      labels
---   vouches(R, VS)     integrity as a SOURCE TAG   -- what R's output carries
---   demands(R, VS)     integrity as a SINK DEMAND  -- what writing R requires
---   dgrant(R, P)       a declassify grant over R
---   needs(B)           `require authority B` -- DR-0063 section 4
---   env(A, S, EP, AR)  one envelope: authority, signature tier, epoch, arms
---   rec(A, EP)         one entry of the run's composition record -- section 4
---
--- MODELLING ASSUMPTION, stated because it is not a fact: every envelope names
--- resources under one spelling, so two envelopes that label `r1` are labelling
--- the same bytes. Two authorities naming one physical resource differently, or
--- one name meaning different bytes on different executors, is DR-0063 O2 --
--- resolving it is prior to composing it.

mod WHIPPLESCRIPT-ENVELOPE-COMPOSITION-DATA is
  protecting BOOL .

  sorts Name Auth Role RoleSet Res Voucher VSet Sig Epoch .
  sorts Arm ArmSet Env EnvSet Rec RecSet Attempt Fact Cfg .
  subsort Role < RoleSet .
  subsort Voucher < VSet .
  subsort Arm < ArmSet .
  subsort Env < EnvSet .
  subsort Rec < RecSet .
  subsort Fact < Cfg .

  ops a1 a2 : -> Auth [ctor] .
  ops nOp nReq : -> Name [ctor] .

  --- DR-0063 section 2. A role reference is qualified by the authority that
  --- issued it, so two envelopes naming `Operator` do not name one principal.
  op q : Auth Name -> Role [ctor] .

  op mtRole : -> RoleSet [ctor] .
  op _|_ : RoleSet RoleSet -> RoleSet [ctor assoc comm id: mtRole] .
  eq P:Role | P:Role = P:Role .

  ops v1 v2 : -> Voucher [ctor] .
  op mtV : -> VSet [ctor] .
  op _;_ : VSet VSet -> VSet [ctor assoc comm id: mtV] .
  eq V:Voucher ; V:Voucher = V:Voucher .

  ops r1 r2 k1 : -> Res [ctor] .
  ops e1 e2 : -> Epoch [ctor] .

  --- The three attestation tiers of spec/information-flow-governance.md's trust
  --- root, plus the domain-tag split DR-0063 section 5 adds. `signedV1` is the
  --- shipped P-256 signature, whose preimage covers signer, key, algorithm and
  --- content hash but NOT the epoch. `signedV2` is the same signature over the
  --- preimage that also binds the epoch and the authority.
  ops signedV2 signedV1 checksumOnly : -> Sig [ctor] .

  --- CONFIDENTIALITY. A label is a set of compartments and a party may read only
  --- if it acts-for every one of them. Delegation is not modelled, so acts-for
  --- is equality here: the empty set is the public bottom, and a singleton is
  --- that party's own compartment. This is `canRead` from the Lean model.
  op canRead : Role RoleSet -> Bool .
  eq canRead(P:Role, mtRole) = true .
  eq canRead(P:Role, C:Role | RS:RoleSet) =
       (P:Role == C:Role) and canRead(P:Role, RS:RoleSet) .

  op inRole : Role RoleSet -> Bool .
  eq inRole(P:Role, P:Role | RS:RoleSet) = true .
  eq inRole(P:Role, RS:RoleSet) = false [owise] .

  op interRole : RoleSet RoleSet -> RoleSet .
  eq interRole(mtRole, RS:RoleSet) = mtRole .
  eq interRole(P:Role | RS1:RoleSet, RS2:RoleSet) =
       if inRole(P:Role, RS2:RoleSet)
       then P:Role | interRole(RS1:RoleSet, RS2:RoleSet)
       else interRole(RS1:RoleSet, RS2:RoleSet) fi .

  op inV : Voucher VSet -> Bool .
  eq inV(V:Voucher, V:Voucher ; VS:VSet) = true .
  eq inV(V:Voucher, VS:VSet) = false [owise] .

  op subV : VSet VSet -> Bool .
  eq subV(mtV, VS:VSet) = true .
  eq subV(V:Voucher ; VS1:VSet, VS2:VSet) =
       inV(V:Voucher, VS2:VSet) and subV(VS1:VSet, VS2:VSet) .

  op interV : VSet VSet -> VSet .
  eq interV(mtV, VS:VSet) = mtV .
  eq interV(V:Voucher ; VS1:VSet, VS2:VSet) =
       if inV(V:Voucher, VS2:VSet)
       then V:Voucher ; interV(VS1:VSet, VS2:VSet)
       else interV(VS1:VSet, VS2:VSet) fi .

  op readers : Res RoleSet -> Arm [ctor] .
  op vouches : Res VSet -> Arm [ctor] .
  op demands : Res VSet -> Arm [ctor] .
  op dgrant : Res Role -> Arm [ctor] .
  op needs : Auth -> Arm [ctor] .
  op mtArm : -> ArmSet [ctor] .
  op _&_ : ArmSet ArmSet -> ArmSet [ctor assoc comm id: mtArm] .

  op env : Auth Sig Epoch ArmSet -> Env [ctor] .
  op mtEnv : -> EnvSet [ctor] .
  op _+_ : EnvSet EnvSet -> EnvSet [ctor assoc comm id: mtEnv] .

  op rec : Auth Epoch -> Rec [ctor] .
  op mtRec : -> RecSet [ctor] .
  op _*_ : RecSet RecSet -> RecSet [ctor assoc comm id: mtRec] .

  vars A B : Auth .   var N : Name .   var S : Sig .   vars EP EP2 : Epoch .
  var AR : ArmSet .   var E : Env .    var ES : EnvSet .
  var RC : RecSet .   vars R K : Res . var P : Role .
  var RS : RoleSet .  var VS : VSet .

  op authOf : Env -> Auth .
  eq authOf(env(A, S, EP, AR)) = A .

  op sigOf : Env -> Sig .
  eq sigOf(env(A, S, EP, AR)) = S .

  op epochOf : Env -> Epoch .
  eq epochOf(env(A, S, EP, AR)) = EP .

  --- `hasReaders` asks whether this envelope LABELS the resource, which is the
  --- ownership question section 3 turns on. It is not the same as the reader set
  --- being non-empty: an empty compartment set is the public bottom, so for the
  --- composition itself no arm and an empty arm coincide, and `readersOf` alone
  --- carries that correctly.
  op hasReaders : Env Res -> Bool .
  eq hasReaders(env(A, S, EP, readers(R, RS) & AR), R) = true .
  eq hasReaders(E, R) = false [owise] .

  op readersOf : Env Res -> RoleSet .
  eq readersOf(env(A, S, EP, readers(R, RS) & AR), R) = RS .
  eq readersOf(E, R) = mtRole [owise] .

  --- Integrity is the other way round: the intersection that composes source
  --- vouchers has the universe as its identity, so "vouches nothing" and "says
  --- nothing" must stay distinguishable.
  op hasVouch : Env Res -> Bool .
  eq hasVouch(env(A, S, EP, vouches(R, VS) & AR), R) = true .
  eq hasVouch(E, R) = false [owise] .

  op vouchOf : Env Res -> VSet .
  eq vouchOf(env(A, S, EP, vouches(R, VS) & AR), R) = VS .
  eq vouchOf(E, R) = mtV [owise] .

  op demandOf : Env Res -> VSet .
  eq demandOf(env(A, S, EP, demands(K, VS) & AR), K) = VS .
  eq demandOf(E, K) = mtV [owise] .

  op grantsD : Env Res Role -> Bool .
  eq grantsD(env(A, S, EP, dgrant(R, P) & AR), R, P) = true .
  eq grantsD(E, R, P) = false [owise] .

  --- DR-0063 section 3. A declassify grant over a resource this envelope does
  --- not itself label is a grant over another party's data. Checked per
  --- envelope, because ownership is local: it does not depend on who else is in
  --- the composition.
  op selfGrantOnly : Env -> Bool .
  eq selfGrantOnly(env(A, S, EP, dgrant(R, P) & AR)) =
       hasReaders(env(A, S, EP, dgrant(R, P) & AR), R)
       and selfGrantOnly(env(A, S, EP, AR)) .
  eq selfGrantOnly(E) = true [owise] .

  op selfGrantsOnly : EnvSet -> Bool .
  eq selfGrantsOnly(mtEnv) = true .
  eq selfGrantsOnly(E + ES) = selfGrantOnly(E) and selfGrantsOnly(ES) .

  --- DR-0063 section 5, first arm: only the authenticated trust root, and only
  --- under the preimage that binds the epoch.
  op allV2 : EnvSet -> Bool .
  eq allV2(mtEnv) = true .
  eq allV2(E + ES) = (sigOf(E) == signedV2) and allV2(ES) .

  --- The sibling policy: accept the shipped signature too. Used by the
  --- -V1-PREIMAGE module below.
  op allSigned : EnvSet -> Bool .
  eq allSigned(mtEnv) = true .
  eq allSigned(E + ES) =
       ((sigOf(E) == signedV2) or (sigOf(E) == signedV1)) and allSigned(ES) .

  --- Second arm: the composition record states an epoch per authority, and it
  --- must be the one the signature covers. Under `signedV1` the preimage does
  --- not reach the epoch, so any stated epoch verifies -- which is what lets a
  --- replayed constituent be presented as a different policy version.
  ---
  --- The record is CHECKED, not consulted: `recStates` asks whether the record
  --- holds this authority at this epoch, and a constituent the record does not
  --- name has no stated epoch at all rather than a defaulted one.
  op recStates : Auth Epoch RecSet -> Bool .
  eq recStates(A, EP, rec(A, EP) * RC) = true .
  eq recStates(A, EP, RC) = false [owise] .

  op epochBound : Env RecSet -> Bool .
  eq epochBound(E, RC) =
       if sigOf(E) == signedV2
       then recStates(authOf(E), epochOf(E), RC)
       else true fi .

  op epochsBound : EnvSet RecSet -> Bool .
  eq epochsBound(mtEnv, RC) = true .
  eq epochsBound(E + ES, RC) = epochBound(E, RC) and epochsBound(ES, RC) .

  --- The lenient lookup, for the -LOOSE-RECORD tooth below: a defaulting
  --- per-authority map, which is what a record consulted rather than checked
  --- gives you. A missing entry defaults, and duplicate entries for one
  --- authority make the lookup itself undetermined -- which is the second half
  --- of why the record is a set obligation and not a map read.
  op statedEpoch : Auth RecSet -> Epoch .
  eq statedEpoch(A, rec(A, EP) * RC) = EP .
  eq statedEpoch(A, RC) = e1 [owise] .

  op epochBoundLoose : Env RecSet -> Bool .
  eq epochBoundLoose(E, RC) =
       if sigOf(E) == signedV2
       then epochOf(E) == statedEpoch(authOf(E), RC)
       else true fi .

  op epochsBoundLoose : EnvSet RecSet -> Bool .
  eq epochsBoundLoose(mtEnv, RC) = true .
  eq epochsBoundLoose(E + ES, RC) =
       epochBoundLoose(E, RC) and epochsBoundLoose(ES, RC) .

  op present : Auth EnvSet -> Bool .
  eq present(A, env(A, S, EP, AR) + ES) = true .
  eq present(A, ES) = false [owise] .

  --- DR-0063 section 4. The record is what the run's evidence cites, so it must
  --- name exactly the set that was checked: every constituent covered, no entry
  --- for an authority the composition does not carry, and no authority named
  --- twice. Envelope duplication stays harmless -- the envelope set is
  --- idempotent -- but RECORD duplication is not, because two entries for one
  --- authority can state different epochs.
  op recNames : Auth RecSet -> Bool .
  eq recNames(A, rec(A, EP) * RC) = true .
  eq recNames(A, RC) = false [owise] .

  op recCovers : EnvSet RecSet -> Bool .
  eq recCovers(mtEnv, RC) = true .
  eq recCovers(E + ES, RC) = recNames(authOf(E), RC) and recCovers(ES, RC) .

  op recOnlyPresent : RecSet EnvSet -> Bool .
  eq recOnlyPresent(mtRec, ES) = true .
  eq recOnlyPresent(rec(A, EP) * RC, ES) =
       present(A, ES) and recOnlyPresent(RC, ES) .

  op recDuplicated : RecSet -> Bool .
  eq recDuplicated(rec(A, EP) * rec(A, EP2) * RC) = true .
  eq recDuplicated(RC) = false [owise] .

  op recordExact : EnvSet RecSet -> Bool .
  eq recordExact(ES, RC) =
       recCovers(ES, RC) and recOnlyPresent(RC, ES)
       and not recDuplicated(RC) .

  op envNeedsMet : Env EnvSet -> Bool .
  eq envNeedsMet(env(A, S, EP, needs(B) & AR), ES) =
       present(B, ES) and envNeedsMet(env(A, S, EP, AR), ES) .
  eq envNeedsMet(E, ES) = true [owise] .

  op needsMet : EnvSet EnvSet -> Bool .
  eq needsMet(mtEnv, ES) = true .
  eq needsMet(E + ES1:EnvSet, ES) =
       envNeedsMet(E, ES) and needsMet(ES1:EnvSet, ES) .

  op read : Res Role -> Attempt [ctor] .
  op write : Res Res -> Attempt [ctor] .

  --- THE SOLO VERDICT. Shared by every module below and never overridden, so a
  --- sibling cannot make a C1 counterexample disappear by quietly weakening the
  --- constituent it is supposed to be compared against.
  op soloCarried : Env Res -> VSet .
  eq soloCarried(E, R) = if hasVouch(E, R) then vouchOf(E, R) else mtV fi .

  op envAccepts : Env Attempt -> Bool .
  eq envAccepts(E, read(R, P)) =
       canRead(P, readersOf(E, R)) or grantsD(E, R, P) .
  eq envAccepts(E, write(R, K)) = subV(demandOf(E, K), soloCarried(E, R)) .

  --- THE COMPOSED ARMS. Both folds of each dual-gated field live here, so a
  --- policy module below differs from the main one in exactly one equation and
  --- the tooth is legible as a diff rather than as a second model.

  --- DR-0063 section 3, applied where the issuer is still known: a downgrade
  --- grant clears the compartments of the envelope that issued it, and that
  --- envelope's contribution to the composed label only. `selfGrantsOnly` has
  --- already made a grant from a non-labelling envelope a hard error, so inside
  --- a well-formed composition this is always the owner clearing its own data.
  op ownReaders : Env Res Role -> RoleSet .
  eq ownReaders(E, R, P) =
       if grantsD(E, R, P) then mtRole else readersOf(E, R) fi .

  --- Confidentiality source tag: UNION of compartments. mtRole is both the
  --- identity of the fold and the public bottom, so an unlabelled resource needs
  --- no guard -- it composes to public, which refuses nothing.
  op readerJoin : EnvSet Res Role -> RoleSet .
  eq readerJoin(mtEnv, R, P) = mtRole .
  eq readerJoin(E + ES, R, P) = ownReaders(E, R, P) | readerJoin(ES, R, P) .

  --- The other way round, for the -INTERSECTED-READERS tooth. Intersection has
  --- the universe as its identity, so this one needs the guard the correct fold
  --- does not.
  op anyReaders : EnvSet Res -> Bool .
  eq anyReaders(mtEnv, R) = false .
  eq anyReaders(E + ES, R) = hasReaders(E, R) or anyReaders(ES, R) .

  op readerMeetRaw : EnvSet Res Role -> RoleSet .
  eq readerMeetRaw(mtEnv, R, P) =
       q(a1, nOp) | q(a1, nReq) | q(a2, nOp) | q(a2, nReq) .
  eq readerMeetRaw(E + ES, R, P) =
       if hasReaders(E, R)
       then interRole(ownReaders(E, R, P), readerMeetRaw(ES, R, P))
       else readerMeetRaw(ES, R, P) fi .

  op readerMeet : EnvSet Res Role -> RoleSet .
  eq readerMeet(ES, R, P) =
       if anyReaders(ES, R) then readerMeetRaw(ES, R, P) else mtRole fi .

  --- Integrity source tag: INTERSECTION over the envelopes that vouch.
  op anyVouch : EnvSet Res -> Bool .
  eq anyVouch(mtEnv, R) = false .
  eq anyVouch(E + ES, R) = hasVouch(E, R) or anyVouch(ES, R) .

  op vouchMeetRaw : EnvSet Res -> VSet .
  eq vouchMeetRaw(mtEnv, R) = v1 ; v2 .
  eq vouchMeetRaw(E + ES, R) =
       if hasVouch(E, R)
       then interV(vouchOf(E, R), vouchMeetRaw(ES, R))
       else vouchMeetRaw(ES, R) fi .

  op vouchMeet : EnvSet Res -> VSet .
  eq vouchMeet(ES, R) = if anyVouch(ES, R) then vouchMeetRaw(ES, R) else mtV fi .

  --- And the other way round, for the -UNION-VOUCHERS tooth.
  op vouchJoin : EnvSet Res -> VSet .
  eq vouchJoin(mtEnv, R) = mtV .
  eq vouchJoin(E + ES, R) = vouchOf(E, R) ; vouchJoin(ES, R) .

  --- Integrity sink demand: UNION, the `required` side.
  op demanded : EnvSet Res -> VSet .
  eq demanded(mtEnv, K) = mtV .
  eq demanded(E + ES, K) = demandOf(E, K) ; demanded(ES, K) .

  --- For the -GLOBAL-GRANTS tooth: an owner's grant applied to the COMPOSED
  --- label rather than to its issuer's own contribution. The ownership check is
  --- honoured -- only a labelling envelope's grant counts -- and it is still
  --- wrong, because on a resource two envelopes label it clears the co-owner's
  --- compartment too.
  op ownerGrants : EnvSet Res Role -> Bool .
  eq ownerGrants(mtEnv, R, P) = false .
  eq ownerGrants(E + ES, R, P) =
       (hasReaders(E, R) and grantsD(E, R, P)) or ownerGrants(ES, R, P) .

  --- The -OPEN-GRANTS sibling substitutes this: any envelope's grant counts.
  op looseGrants : EnvSet Res Role -> Bool .
  eq looseGrants(mtEnv, R, P) = false .
  eq looseGrants(E + ES, R, P) = grantsD(E, R, P) or looseGrants(ES, R, P) .

  op composition : EnvSet RecSet -> Fact [ctor] .
  op attempt : Attempt -> Fact [ctor] .
  op admitted : Attempt -> Fact [ctor] .
  op soloRefuses : Auth Attempt -> Fact [ctor] .
  op compositionError : -> Fact [ctor] .
  op none : -> Cfg [ctor] .
  op __ : Cfg Cfg -> Cfg [ctor assoc comm id: none] .

  var X : Attempt .
  eq admitted(X) admitted(X) = admitted(X) .
  eq soloRefuses(A, X) soloRefuses(A, X) = soloRefuses(A, X) .
  eq compositionError compositionError = compositionError .
endm

--- THE COMPOSITION UNDER TEST.
mod WHIPPLESCRIPT-ENVELOPE-COMPOSITION is
  protecting WHIPPLESCRIPT-ENVELOPE-COMPOSITION-DATA .

  var E : Env .   var ES : EnvSet .   var RC : RecSet .
  vars R K : Res . var P : Role .     var X : Attempt .

  op meetAccepts : EnvSet Attempt -> Bool .
  eq meetAccepts(ES, read(R, P)) = canRead(P, readerJoin(ES, R, P)) .
  eq meetAccepts(ES, write(R, K)) = subV(demanded(ES, K), vouchMeet(ES, R)) .

  --- DR-0063 sections 3, 4 and 5. Fail-closed and NAMED: an ill-formed
  --- composition produces `compositionError` rather than dropping the offending
  --- arm, because a silently dropped grant is one a party goes on believing it
  --- holds.
  op wellFormed : EnvSet RecSet -> Bool .
  eq wellFormed(ES, RC) =
       allV2(ES) and epochsBound(ES, RC) and recordExact(ES, RC)
       and selfGrantsOnly(ES) and needsMet(ES, ES) .

  crl [meet-admit] : composition(ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(ES, RC) attempt(X) admitted(X)
    if wellFormed(ES, RC) and meetAccepts(ES, X) .

  crl [ill-formed] : composition(ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(ES, RC) attempt(X) compositionError
    if not wellFormed(ES, RC) .

  --- The constituent verdicts, recorded alongside the composed one so that a C1
  --- counterexample is a single reachable state rather than a comparison run by
  --- hand between two searches.
  crl [solo-refuse] : composition(E + ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(E + ES, RC) attempt(X) soloRefuses(authOf(E), X)
    if not envAccepts(E, X) .
endm

--- TOOTH 1, SOUND_MEET on the confidentiality arm. Compartment sets composed by
--- intersection instead of union -- the direction that reads as "restrict to
--- what both allow" and is exactly backwards for a conjunctive set. Two parties
--- each attach their own compartment to one resource, the intersection is empty,
--- and empty is the public bottom: a label neither constituent would have
--- accepted admits everyone.
mod WHIPPLESCRIPT-ENVELOPE-COMPOSITION-INTERSECTED-READERS is
  protecting WHIPPLESCRIPT-ENVELOPE-COMPOSITION-DATA .

  var E : Env .   var ES : EnvSet .   var RC : RecSet .
  vars R K : Res . var P : Role .     var X : Attempt .

  op meetAccepts : EnvSet Attempt -> Bool .
  eq meetAccepts(ES, read(R, P)) = canRead(P, readerMeet(ES, R, P)) .
  eq meetAccepts(ES, write(R, K)) = subV(demanded(ES, K), vouchMeet(ES, R)) .

  op wellFormed : EnvSet RecSet -> Bool .
  eq wellFormed(ES, RC) =
       allV2(ES) and epochsBound(ES, RC) and recordExact(ES, RC)
       and selfGrantsOnly(ES) and needsMet(ES, ES) .

  crl [meet-admit] : composition(ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(ES, RC) attempt(X) admitted(X)
    if wellFormed(ES, RC) and meetAccepts(ES, X) .

  crl [ill-formed] : composition(ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(ES, RC) attempt(X) compositionError
    if not wellFormed(ES, RC) .

  crl [solo-refuse] : composition(E + ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(E + ES, RC) attempt(X) soloRefuses(authOf(E), X)
    if not envAccepts(E, X) .
endm

--- TOOTH 2, SOUND_MEET on the integrity arm. Source vouchers composed by union
--- instead of intersection: the composed source carries what ANY party vouched,
--- so one party's lower opinion of a shared source is discarded and its own
--- sink demand is met over its own refusal.
mod WHIPPLESCRIPT-ENVELOPE-COMPOSITION-UNION-VOUCHERS is
  protecting WHIPPLESCRIPT-ENVELOPE-COMPOSITION-DATA .

  var E : Env .   var ES : EnvSet .   var RC : RecSet .
  vars R K : Res . var P : Role .     var X : Attempt .

  op meetAccepts : EnvSet Attempt -> Bool .
  eq meetAccepts(ES, read(R, P)) = canRead(P, readerJoin(ES, R, P)) .
  eq meetAccepts(ES, write(R, K)) = subV(demanded(ES, K), vouchJoin(ES, R)) .

  op wellFormed : EnvSet RecSet -> Bool .
  eq wellFormed(ES, RC) =
       allV2(ES) and epochsBound(ES, RC) and recordExact(ES, RC)
       and selfGrantsOnly(ES) and needsMet(ES, ES) .

  crl [meet-admit] : composition(ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(ES, RC) attempt(X) admitted(X)
    if wellFormed(ES, RC) and meetAccepts(ES, X) .

  crl [ill-formed] : composition(ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(ES, RC) attempt(X) compositionError
    if not wellFormed(ES, RC) .

  crl [solo-refuse] : composition(E + ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(E + ES, RC) attempt(X) soloRefuses(authOf(E), X)
    if not envAccepts(E, X) .
endm

--- TOOTH 3, NO_ROLE_ALIASING. A compartment is satisfied by matching its NAME,
--- which is what a bare unqualified role string gives you. One authority's
--- Operator then clears another authority's compartment, having been granted
--- nothing by anyone.
mod WHIPPLESCRIPT-ENVELOPE-COMPOSITION-ALIASED-ROLES is
  protecting WHIPPLESCRIPT-ENVELOPE-COMPOSITION-DATA .

  vars A B : Auth .  vars M N : Name .
  var E : Env .   var ES : EnvSet .   var RC : RecSet .
  vars R K : Res . var P : Role .     var RS : RoleSet .  var X : Attempt .

  op canReadByName : Role RoleSet -> Bool .
  eq canReadByName(P, mtRole) = true .
  eq canReadByName(q(A, N), q(B, M) | RS) =
       (N == M) and canReadByName(q(A, N), RS) .

  op meetAccepts : EnvSet Attempt -> Bool .
  eq meetAccepts(ES, read(R, P)) = canReadByName(P, readerJoin(ES, R, P)) .
  eq meetAccepts(ES, write(R, K)) = subV(demanded(ES, K), vouchMeet(ES, R)) .

  op wellFormed : EnvSet RecSet -> Bool .
  eq wellFormed(ES, RC) =
       allV2(ES) and epochsBound(ES, RC) and recordExact(ES, RC)
       and selfGrantsOnly(ES) and needsMet(ES, ES) .

  crl [meet-admit] : composition(ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(ES, RC) attempt(X) admitted(X)
    if wellFormed(ES, RC) and meetAccepts(ES, X) .

  crl [ill-formed] : composition(ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(ES, RC) attempt(X) compositionError
    if not wellFormed(ES, RC) .

  crl [solo-refuse] : composition(E + ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(E + ES, RC) attempt(X) soloRefuses(authOf(E), X)
    if not envAccepts(E, X) .
endm

--- TOOTH 4, NO_CROSS_GRANT. Ownership is dropped from both places it appears: a
--- foreign declassify grant no longer makes the composition ill-formed, and it
--- authorizes a crossing on the resource it names. This is the "silently
--- ignored" alternative built out honestly -- the weaker of the two failures,
--- and it still hands one party a downgrade over another's data.
mod WHIPPLESCRIPT-ENVELOPE-COMPOSITION-OPEN-GRANTS is
  protecting WHIPPLESCRIPT-ENVELOPE-COMPOSITION-DATA .

  var E : Env .   var ES : EnvSet .   var RC : RecSet .
  vars R K : Res . var P : Role .     var X : Attempt .

  op meetAccepts : EnvSet Attempt -> Bool .
  eq meetAccepts(ES, read(R, P)) =
       canRead(P, readerJoin(ES, R, P)) or looseGrants(ES, R, P) .
  eq meetAccepts(ES, write(R, K)) = subV(demanded(ES, K), vouchMeet(ES, R)) .

  op wellFormed : EnvSet RecSet -> Bool .
  eq wellFormed(ES, RC) =
       allV2(ES) and epochsBound(ES, RC) and recordExact(ES, RC)
       and needsMet(ES, ES) .

  crl [meet-admit] : composition(ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(ES, RC) attempt(X) admitted(X)
    if wellFormed(ES, RC) and meetAccepts(ES, X) .

  crl [ill-formed] : composition(ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(ES, RC) attempt(X) compositionError
    if not wellFormed(ES, RC) .

  crl [solo-refuse] : composition(E + ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(E + ES, RC) attempt(X) soloRefuses(authOf(E), X)
    if not envAccepts(E, X) .
endm

--- TOOTH 5, SOUND_MEET on the grant arm. A downgrade grant applied to the
--- COMPOSED label rather than to the compartments of the envelope that issued
--- it. Section 3's "grants are not intersected" is true, and this is the wrong
--- reading of it: the ownership check is honoured -- only a labelling envelope's
--- grant counts -- and on a resource two envelopes both label, the issuer's
--- grant clears its co-owner's compartment as well as its own. The same failure
--- -OPEN-GRANTS reaches by dropping the ownership check, reached here while
--- passing it, which is why passing it is not the property.
mod WHIPPLESCRIPT-ENVELOPE-COMPOSITION-GLOBAL-GRANTS is
  protecting WHIPPLESCRIPT-ENVELOPE-COMPOSITION-DATA .

  var E : Env .   var ES : EnvSet .   var RC : RecSet .
  vars R K : Res . var P : Role .     var X : Attempt .

  op meetAccepts : EnvSet Attempt -> Bool .
  eq meetAccepts(ES, read(R, P)) =
       canRead(P, readerJoin(ES, R, P)) or ownerGrants(ES, R, P) .
  eq meetAccepts(ES, write(R, K)) = subV(demanded(ES, K), vouchMeet(ES, R)) .

  op wellFormed : EnvSet RecSet -> Bool .
  eq wellFormed(ES, RC) =
       allV2(ES) and epochsBound(ES, RC) and recordExact(ES, RC)
       and selfGrantsOnly(ES) and needsMet(ES, ES) .

  crl [meet-admit] : composition(ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(ES, RC) attempt(X) admitted(X)
    if wellFormed(ES, RC) and meetAccepts(ES, X) .

  crl [ill-formed] : composition(ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(ES, RC) attempt(X) compositionError
    if not wellFormed(ES, RC) .

  crl [solo-refuse] : composition(E + ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(E + ES, RC) attempt(X) soloRefuses(authOf(E), X)
    if not envAccepts(E, X) .
endm

--- TOOTH 6, OMISSION_WIDENS. The composition record is consulted as a defaulting
--- per-authority map rather than checked as a set: a constituent the record does
--- not name gets a default epoch, an entry naming an absent authority is never
--- looked at, and a doubly-named authority resolves to whichever entry the
--- lookup reaches. The run is then admitted while citing evidence for a set it
--- was not checked under, which is the shorter-record case section 4 names.
mod WHIPPLESCRIPT-ENVELOPE-COMPOSITION-LOOSE-RECORD is
  protecting WHIPPLESCRIPT-ENVELOPE-COMPOSITION-DATA .

  var E : Env .   var ES : EnvSet .   var RC : RecSet .
  vars R K : Res . var P : Role .     var X : Attempt .

  op meetAccepts : EnvSet Attempt -> Bool .
  eq meetAccepts(ES, read(R, P)) = canRead(P, readerJoin(ES, R, P)) .
  eq meetAccepts(ES, write(R, K)) = subV(demanded(ES, K), vouchMeet(ES, R)) .

  op wellFormed : EnvSet RecSet -> Bool .
  eq wellFormed(ES, RC) =
       allV2(ES) and epochsBoundLoose(ES, RC)
       and selfGrantsOnly(ES) and needsMet(ES, ES) .

  crl [meet-admit] : composition(ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(ES, RC) attempt(X) admitted(X)
    if wellFormed(ES, RC) and meetAccepts(ES, X) .

  crl [ill-formed] : composition(ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(ES, RC) attempt(X) compositionError
    if not wellFormed(ES, RC) .

  crl [solo-refuse] : composition(E + ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(E + ES, RC) attempt(X) soloRefuses(authOf(E), X)
    if not envAccepts(E, X) .
endm

--- TOOTH 7, the epoch. The shipped P-256 preimage covers signer, key, algorithm
--- and content hash but not the epoch, and this module admits it. The same valid
--- signature then verifies under whatever epoch the composition record states,
--- so a constituent can be replayed as a different -- including an earlier --
--- policy version, which is the non-retroactivity claim section 4's record is
--- meant to carry.
mod WHIPPLESCRIPT-ENVELOPE-COMPOSITION-V1-PREIMAGE is
  protecting WHIPPLESCRIPT-ENVELOPE-COMPOSITION-DATA .

  var E : Env .   var ES : EnvSet .   var RC : RecSet .
  vars R K : Res . var P : Role .     var X : Attempt .

  op meetAccepts : EnvSet Attempt -> Bool .
  eq meetAccepts(ES, read(R, P)) = canRead(P, readerJoin(ES, R, P)) .
  eq meetAccepts(ES, write(R, K)) = subV(demanded(ES, K), vouchMeet(ES, R)) .

  op wellFormed : EnvSet RecSet -> Bool .
  eq wellFormed(ES, RC) =
       allSigned(ES) and epochsBound(ES, RC) and recordExact(ES, RC)
       and selfGrantsOnly(ES) and needsMet(ES, ES) .

  crl [meet-admit] : composition(ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(ES, RC) attempt(X) admitted(X)
    if wellFormed(ES, RC) and meetAccepts(ES, X) .

  crl [ill-formed] : composition(ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(ES, RC) attempt(X) compositionError
    if not wellFormed(ES, RC) .

  crl [solo-refuse] : composition(E + ES, RC) attempt(X)
    => composition(E + ES, RC) attempt(X) soloRefuses(authOf(E), X)
    if not envAccepts(E, X) .
endm
